<article class="env-lemma" id="0CRK">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0CRK">Lemma <span data-tag="0CRK">13.33.8</span>.</a> Let $\mathcal{D}$ be a triangulated category having countable direct sums. Let $\mathcal{A}$ be an abelian category with exact colimits over $\mathbf{N}$. Let $H : \mathcal{D} \to \mathcal{A}$ be a homological functor commuting with countable direct sums. Then $H(\text{hocolim} K_ n) = \mathop{\mathrm{colim}}\nolimits H(K_ n)$ for any system of objects of $\mathcal{D}$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Write $K = \text{hocolim} K_ n$. Apply $H$ to the defining distinguished triangle to get 
    <p>
      <div class="equation">
  \[  \bigoplus H(K_ n) \to \bigoplus H(K_ n) \to H(K) \to \bigoplus H(K_ n[1]) \to \bigoplus H(K_ n[1])  \]
</div>
    <p>
       where the first map is given by $1 - H(f_ n)$ and the last map is given by $1 - H(f_ n[1])$. Apply Lemma <a href="/tag/093W" data-tag="093W">13.33.6</a> to see that this proves the lemma. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>